# Settings for local runs: copy to .env (git-ignored). vite.config.ts reads it
# at startup; a variable already set in the shell wins over the file.
# Everything here is optional; with no .env the dev server listens on
# localhost:8780 and serves no game data from disk.

# Listen on every interface so a phone or second PC can open the dev server.
# UBIQUITOUS_LAN=1

# Dev server port; change it to run two checkouts side by side.
# UBIQUITOUS_CLIENT_PORT=8780

# Port of the game server to dial, overriding the `server=` line of
# public/config.txt (and the address the dev server forwards phones to).
# UBIQUITOUS_SERVER_PORT=8781

# Directories (separated by `;`) holding your extracted packs or .ipa, which
# the /dev/ pages read over /@fs/. Never put an absolute path in a committed file.
# UBIQUITOUS_PACK_DIR=

# Required to combine UBIQUITOUS_PACK_DIR with UBIQUITOUS_LAN=1: it offers your
# game files to the whole network.
# UBIQUITOUS_LAN_PACKS=1

# Game data for the tests that want it; unset, those tests skip.
# UBIQUITOUS_PACK=
# UBIQUITOUS_IPA=
